Gonna keep trying to go with the daily writing stuff

Sunday I was able to do a lot of personal study which was nice, and during
the Go and Do experience I rewatched =E2=80=9Cthe phone call=E2=80=9D and a=
 very old church
video called =E2=80=9Cman's search for happiness=E2=80=9D. It was fun to ha=
ve a bit of
nostalgia with the phone call, but beyond that I learned a lot about the
value of lasting relationships and about how central the family is in the
Gospel

Monday was also good, me and my companion had our first 25 minute HOA and
it definitely didn't go perfectly, but it was decent. (IDK if I've even
explained what an =E2=80=9CHOA=E2=80=9D [Helping Others Appointment] is, bu=
t in case I
haven't it's basically someone whose native language is Japanese in this
case, and is either acting or genuinely seeking to know more about the
church (much less likely lol), and we basically practice teaching to them)
Monday I also got a lot more Japanese practice in throughout the 6 hours of
classes. We learned a lot about making and asking questions in Japanese,
and it's crazy how flip flopped the sentences get when compared to English
=F0=9F=98=B5=E2=80=8D=F0=9F=92=AB

Tuesday we had our General Authority devotional and we got to hear from
Elder and Sister Bassett, which was really neat. I loved both of their
talks, and I feel like my main takeaway from what I heard was that one of
the best things we can use our time for as members of the church
(especially at this age) is being a missionary. We are in the water, and
we're trying to help others find for themselves how it feels, through
baptism especially. Also got me thinking about the themesong for The Chosen
=F0=9F=98=82

I allllso wrote another poem in the 5 minutes of journal time we had before
our group devotional breakdown: (will have to send it next week sorry,
short on time =F0=9F=98=85)

Wednesday was a good day (any day where I'm learning is a good day), but
very exhausting, I think I might be catching a cold again and it was not
very fun talking for such a long time.

Thursday

Felt a little worse on Thursday, but nothing crazy. We learned a lot of
different sentence strengtheners, one of which (=E3=81=A8=E3=81=84=E3=81=86=
) genuinely can't
cohesively translate very well into English which makes it pretty tricky to
learn =F0=9F=98=85 We've pretty much learned all the pieces of sentence str=
ucture
stuff but we are just now trying to incorporate it together.

Friday was good, but I definitely woke up super stuffy and runny which was
not very fun. The rest of the day was aight though.

P-day/Saturday was good, but my voice was almost gone. We had one morning
class and then had the rest of the day to shine shoes, do laundry, play
volleyball and buy some cough drops (as well as some BYU creamery ice
cream) super excited for Sunday and Tuesday, but I'm pretty doubtful as to
my singing capabilities in the choir practices =F0=9F=98=85 I was waaaay to=
o loud and
I'm pretty certain I will not be able to talk at all tomorrow=E2=80=A6

Well thanks again for this issue of Elder Killians issues. I'm hoping I'll
feel a lot better next week, very exciting that we only have a couple weeks
left at the MTC =F0=9F=91=80 I cannot wait for Japan (or likely a reassignm=
ent lol)

Love you guys!!!!!!!!!!!

-Elder Killian

Spiritual Afterthought

Alma 34

16 And thus mercy can satisfy the demands of justice, and encircles them in
the arms of safety, while he that exercises no faith unto repentance is
exposed to the whole law of the demands of justice; therefore only unto him
that has faith unto repentance is brought about the great and eternal plan
of redemption.

Pretty to the point scripture, which I like. Faith is so emphasized in
religion and is such a basic step that I feel like people sometimes forget
just how crucial it is. having faith in the first place Is a challenge, but
I think that strengthening It rather than just letting it sit there is
easier said than done. Keep at it!!

Bye =F0=9F=91=8B

--000000000000cf9abd06207aebf1
